          "suggestions": "The agent correctly identified the asset/site, pulled the acetylene, co and hydrogen series for the requested window via iot.history, and reported values accurately (4 samples per channel, all non-null). However, the core requirement \u2014 running a proper anomaly detection model via tsfm.run_recipe with task tsfm_anomaly_detection \u2014 was not accomplished. The agent stopped after find_models returned an empty catalog and reported that it could not materialize the series into a dataset file; it also skipped tsfm.data_quality and tsfm.profile_series. It then applied the manual >50%-above-mean fallback even though the stated fallback condition (fewer than 4 non-null samples) was explicitly not met, which contradicts the user's instructions (though the agent was transparent about this). The 'window looks stable' conclusion is therefore not grounded in a detector results_file as expected. To rectify: use the recipe_template guidance to build an inline SubLOF estimator (task tsfm_anomaly_detection), materialize the retrieved series into the TSFM work directory (or use whatever dataset-path mechanism the environment provides), run run_recipe, and report per-channel anomaly timestamps/values/n_anomalies from the results_file before applying the escalation logic. Also call tsfm.data_quality to formally confirm non-null counts. The reference to an 'unattributed SubLOF run earlier today' should be avoided unless it is clearly tied to a tool call in this session; it adds confusion without evidential value."
